# npm's Arborist crashes with "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')" while
# recursing into vitest's own peer-dependency set (npm 10.9.8 / Node 22). It is reached via
# @angular/build's *optional* `vitest: ^4.0.8` peer: this repo is on vitest 5, so Arborist
# resolves the unsatisfied peer, fetches vitest 4.1.11's manifest, and dies walking its peer
# set. An npm/Arborist bug, not something specific to this repo - legacy-peer-deps sidesteps
# that resolution path entirely. Reproduces on a clean install (no node_modules, no lockfile);
# an incremental install over an existing tree happens to get far enough not to hit it.
# Removable once npm ships a fix, or once @angular/build widens that peer to vitest 5 - if
# `npm install` starts crashing that way again after removing it, that's why.
legacy-peer-deps=true
